---
import LandingLayout from '@/layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import { business, whatsappWith } from '@/data/business';

// We do not keep a G63 in the standing fleet. Every mention on this page is
// framed as sourced-on-request; nothing here promises a car we hold.
const wa = whatsappWith("Hi, I'd like to check G63 availability and rates for my dates.");
---
<LandingLayout
  title="G-Wagon Rental Miami | Lussaro Collection"
  description="Mercedes-AMG G63 in Miami, sourced on request for your dates. Message us on WhatsApp for availability and rates, or browse the cars we keep on hand."
  h1="G-Wagon Rental Miami"
  intro="The Mercedes-AMG G63 is sourced on request for your dates rather than kept on the lot. Message us on WhatsApp and we will confirm availability and rates."
  fleetHeading="Also in our Miami fleet"
  ctaTitle="Ask about the G-Wagon"
>
  <h2>How a G-Wagon booking works here</h2>
  <p>We do not hold a Mercedes-AMG G63 in the standing fleet. When someone wants one we source it for their dates, which means availability and price depend on the window you need rather than on a published rate. <a href={wa}>Message us on WhatsApp</a> with your dates and we will come back with both.</p>
  <p>If your dates are fixed and short-notice, say so up front — sourcing takes longer than handing over a car we already have, and it is better to know early whether it is realistic.</p>

  <h3>What the G63 offers</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Unmistakable boxy silhouette, and the curb appeal that comes with it.</li>
    <li>Twin-turbo V8 power with AMG engineering.</li>
    <li>A tall, upright cabin that seats four in comfort.</li>
    <li>Ride height that shrugs off ramps and speed bumps.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Available now instead</h3>
  <p>If you would rather book something today, the cars above are ours and ready on live dates. The <a href="/cars/mercedes-maybach-gls-600">Maybach GLS 600</a> is the closest in spirit — a large Mercedes SUV built around its back seat — and the <a href="/cars/lamborghini-urus">Lamborghini Urus</a> covers the same want-presence-and-space brief with considerably more noise. Both appear on our <a href="/luxury-suv-rental-miami">luxury SUV comparison</a>.</p>
  <p>For the full picture, see <a href="/exotic-car-rental-miami">exotic car rental in Miami</a> or the complete <a href="/fleet">fleet</a>.</p>

  <h3>What you can rely on</h3>
  <p>Whatever we source, the terms are the ones published on our <a href="/pricing">rate card</a>: the deposit, the mileage allowance and the delivery fees do not change because a car came in specially. You will have the rate in writing before anything is committed.</p>
</LandingLayout>
